  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving the health sector coordination, information and management systems for sustainability - Lao (Peoples Democratic Republic) (01-Jan-2016-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lao (Peoples Democratic Republic), RSSH, Ministry of Health of the Lao People&apos;s Democratic Republic (MOH)This program has the following goals: To strengthen the coordination, information and management capacities of the Lao PDR Health System to improve access to basic health care and financial protection by 2020.. The objectives of this program are: Objective: To improve quality and use of the National Strategic Health Information System, including HIV, TB and Malaria.  Objective: To improve the financial reporting of HIV, TB and malaria programs through the MOH financial reporting system.  Objective: To strengthen mechanism for effective integration of 3 diseases into the health system management in provinces with HIV, TB and malaria activities with a view of reaching UHC.  Objective: To strengthen the linkages and health care services between facility based and community based health workers through the implementation of the VHW policy.  Objective: To Strengthen the overall PSM system to improve access to quality assured medicines and promote the rational use of medicines and medical products</narrative>
  </description>
